cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Tacitus Policy Workbench in research, evaluation, or derivative work, please cite this repository and its documented upstream dependencies."
title: "Tacitus Policy Workbench"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Giulio
    family-names: Catanzariti
    affiliation: TACITUS
    email: hello@tacitus.me
repository-code: "https://github.com/sargonxg/tacitus-political-policy-second-brain"
url: "https://www.tacitus.me"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Tacitus Policy Workbench is an experimental local-first environment for
  evidence-grounded policy and political analysis. It adapts EdgeQuake with
  domain-specific policy objects, attributed claims, review receipts,
  question-bounded context, analytical output contracts, and portable context
  capsules.
keywords:
  - policy research
  - political analysis
  - local-first
  - knowledge graphs
  - provenance
  - human review
